<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otakars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1056">1056</a>–<a href="/years/1192">1192</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Traungauer</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Otakars were a noble dynasty, counts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steyr">Steyr</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-austria">Upper Austria</a>, who ruled the Carantanian March from 1056. They made it independent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carinthia">Carinthia</a>, and the land took its name, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a>, from their castle of Steyr. Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> raised Ottokar IV to duke in 1180, and the line ended with his death in 1192.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otakars.jpg" alt="Otakars" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giltsbeach · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_Ottokar_III_of_Styria.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
